WebGPU: integer and 16-bit normalized formats have WebGPU's sample types

A bind group layout takes a texture's sample type from the format table, which said float for every integer
format and for the 16-bit normalized ones. WebGPU gives integer formats uint or sint, and r16unorm, rg16unorm,
rgba16unorm and their snorm forms unfilterable-float only, so a shader declaring an integer texture, and any
binding of a 16-bit normalized texture, failed validation. Samplers of integer formats become non-filtering,
as those of unfilterable formats already did.

